# Development defaults, so a fresh clone runs without hunting for config.
# Every VITE_* value is compiled into the browser bundle and is therefore
# public by definition — never put a real secret in this file.
#
# Deliberately EMPTY, not the API host. Empty keeps API calls relative, so they
# go to your own dev server and are proxied to the API from there (see the
# proxy block in vite.config.ts). That matters because the API's CORS allowlist
# accepts only http://localhost:5173 and http://localhost:3000 — so calling it
# directly breaks the moment Vite moves to 5174 because 5173 was busy, or you
# open 127.0.0.1 instead of localhost. Both show up as "Server maintenance".
#
# Setting a real URL here re-introduces exactly that failure.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
